Phonon CPU + Video

Upstream project: Phonon by Fermion Research and its contributors.
Original repository: https://github.com/fermionresearch/phonon
Upstream CPU container:
https://github.com/fermionresearch/phonon/pkgs/container/phonon-cpu

Credit for the speech models, CPU inference engine, original CLI/API, and base
container belongs to Fermion Research and the upstream contributors. This
independent project adds FFmpeg media preparation, an adapter for video,
packaging, and tests. It is not an official or endorsed Fermion Research release.

The adapter does not contain copied upstream source. The image includes upstream
software, distro FFmpeg, and Python wrapper dependencies.

The inspected fermion-research 0.2.11 wheel metadata declares Apache-2.0.
The wheel includes LICENSE and NOTICE files. Preserve the original files in the
upstream installation. The upstream NOTICE credits Fermion Research,
Qwen/Alibaba/Hugging Face, and the Parakeet architecture by NVIDIA.
Before you distribute a release, inspect the packages in the pinned container.
The current source does not prove which software the image contains.

This project's source and image do not include model weights. Model repositories
have their own licenses and attribution requirements. The inspected upstream
NOTICE identifies Phonon-2 / NVIDIA Parakeet-derived weights as CC-BY-4.0.
It identifies Phonon-1 / Qwen-derived weights as Apache-2.0. Do not assume that
these entries apply to every model or the current Phonon-2.5 release.
Before deployment or redistribution, check the exact model revision and
preserve the model license and NOTICE.

FFmpeg distribution terms depend on the build and linked codecs. Retain the
installed Debian package copyright and license files under /usr/share/doc.
Before you distribute the combined image, review these items:
- ffmpeg -buildconf
- Package source availability
- GPL/LGPL terms
- Applicable codec obligations
https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

Python wrapper dependencies have separate licenses. Record their resolved
versions in requirements.lock and uv.lock. Keep package license metadata in
the wrapper virtual environment. Before release, generate and review an image SBOM.

The new adapter code is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
See LICENSE for the full terms. Third-party software and model weights retain
their own licenses. Third-party distribution review and model/fixture provenance
review are still required before you release the combined image.
